# Timeline

## Abstract

The verified chronology of the relationship with {{ project_title }}: what
happened, when, and how we know it. Every entry carries a source, so a later
reader can re-check it instead of trusting it. This is also the chronological
index into [`meetings/`](meetings/) — each meeting gets a line here linking to
its note.

**Append at the bottom; never rewrite an entry.** If an entry turns out to be
wrong, add a corrected one with today's date saying so. The value of a timeline
is that it shows what we believed at the time.

**State the timezone once and normalise to it.** Mail archives usually store UTC
while quoted mail headers are already local, and mixing the two silently shifts
events by an hour or two — enough to invert who replied first.

